Translation patch: the binlog flags types as plain structs

Change: `EventFlags`, `SemiSyncFlags`, `GtidFlags`, `RowsEventFlags`, `UserVarFlags` (binlog/consts.rs) and `Flags2`, `SqlMode` (constants.rs) switch from `my_bitflags!` to `my_plain_bitflags!` (patch 20), dropping `Debug` from their `derive` lists.
Why: As in patch 20: `bitflags!` goes through the external `bitflags::Bits`/`Flags` traits, which Aeneas does not model; `RawFlags<T, _>` of these types appear in the binlog events.
Behaviour: Identical, see patch 20 (same API, same bodies, same `Debug` output).

